1
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:54,000
An epic of miniature proportions.

2
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:42,000
A Bug's Life is a family, animation, adventure film directed by John Lasseter.

3
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:30,000
On behalf of "oppressed bugs everywhere," an inventive ant named Flik hires a troupe of warrior bugs to defend
his bustling colony from a horde of freeloading grasshoppers led by the evil-minded Hopper.

4
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:18,000
Flik (voice), played by Dave Foley.

5
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Hopper (voice), played by Kevin Spacey.

6
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:54,000
Atta (voice), played by Julia Louis-Dreyfus.

7
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:42,000
Dot (voice), played by Hayden Panettiere.

8
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:30,000
Queen (voice), played by Phyllis Diller.

9
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:18,000
Molt (voice), played by Richard Kind.

10
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
A Bug's Life (stylized in all lowercase) is a 1998 American animated comedy film
produced by Pixar Animation Studios for Walt Disney Pictures.

11
00:41:48,000 --> 00:41:54,000
It was directed by John Lasseter, written by Andrew Stanton, Donald McEnery, and Bob Shaw, from a story conceived by Lasseter,
Stanton, and Joe Ranft, and stars the voices of Dave Foley, Kevin Spacey, Julia Louis-Dreyfus, and Hayden Panettiere.

12
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:42,000
In the film, a misfit anthropomorphic ant named Flik looks for "tough warriors" to save
his ant colony from a protection racket run by a gang of grasshoppers.

13
00:49:24,000 --> 00:49:30,000
However, the "warriors" he brings back are a troupe of Circus Bugs.

14
00:53:12,000 --> 00:53:18,000
The film's plot was initially inspired by Aesop's
fable The Ant and the Grasshopper.

15
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
Production on A Bug's Life began shortly after the release of Toy Story in 1995.

16
01:00:48,000 --> 01:00:54,000
The ants in the film were redesigned to be more appealing, and Pixar's
animation unit employed technical innovations in computer animation.

17
01:04:36,000 --> 01:04:42,000
Randy Newman composed the music for the film.

18
01:08:24,000 --> 01:08:30,000
During production, a controversial public feud erupted between Steve Jobs and Lasseter of Pixar and DreamWorks co-founder
Jeffrey Katzenberg due to the parallel production of his similar film Antz, which was released the month prior.

19
01:12:12,000 --> 01:12:18,000
A Bug's Life premiered at the El Capitan Theatre in Los Angeles on November
14, 1998, and was released in the United States on November 25.

20
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
It received positive reviews for its animation, story, humor, and voice acting.

21
01:19:48,000 --> 01:19:54,000
It became a commercial success, having grossed $363 million at the box office.

22
01:23:36,000 --> 01:23:42,000
It was the first film to be digitally transferred frame-by-frame and released
on DVD, and has been released multiple times on home video.

23
01:27:24,000 --> 01:27:30,000
The film explores themes of fight, circus, winter, ant-hill, ant.

24
01:31:12,000 --> 01:31:18,000
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
